    "narrative": "For the Zurich Zebras on this October 24th, our offensive output is consolidated into a lean two-man effort against Henderson and Rasmussen. **Christian Yelich** earns the top spot today with a score of 53.93, benefiting significantly from a +13% dynamic platoon boost against the right-handed Rasmussen. While the opposing arm\u2019s 3.30 xERA is respectable, **Christian Yelich** remains our most reliable anchor in the 3-hole, providing the necessary stability in AVG and counting stats. **Junior Caminero** follows closely with a 53.53 score; despite a -19% penalty due to Henderson's high-tier command, his placement in the cleanup spot and a favorable platoon profile keep him in the green, offering enough upside to warrant the start.\n\nThe bench remains stagnant today, as key speed assets like **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Trea Turner**, and **Caleb Durbin** are unavailable due to team off-days. This lack of depth makes the binary decision regarding our remaining roster\u2014which includes **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez**\u2014moot, as none are active today. We are essentially riding out a quiet slate, avoiding any usage of our game caps while our primary sluggers, including the sidelined **Yordan Alvarez**, rest. With no high-variance weather or lineup uncertainty affecting the two active starters, our focus remains on monitoring the efficiency of **Christian Yelich** and **Junior Caminero** to ensure we don't bleed points against tough SP matchups.",
